# counter harness. One force call is one clean energy and gradient.
# Each analytic Hessian costs one force call per coordinate.
# gradient_calls is the harness energy and gradient. hessian_calls counts matrices. hessian_force_calls is matrices times the dimension. force_calls is their sum.
# Noise is added after the call. A repeated coordinate keeps that sample.
# The index uses the clean Hessian. Six rigid modes are removed.
# A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# Energy and Kabsch RMSD are not applied: the problem file has no per-start reference.
# Default profile at sigma 0. Newton and dogleg call the analytic Hessian of the clean force. Positive sigma has no template: the noisy force is not that gradient.
